WEBVTT

00:01.900 --> 00:03.400
<i>What's next again?</i>

00:04.180 --> 00:06.400
<i>The PR campaign for that new horror game.</i>

00:06.520 --> 00:09.610
<b>Whee!</b>

00:07.190 --> 00:09.600
<i>We got a demo version, so 
let's all play together!</i>

00:09.600 --> 00:11.490
<i>If you want to do PR right,</i>

00:11.490 --> 00:14.170
<i>you really need to understand the product.</i>

00:14.170 --> 00:16.310
<i>I'm not really into games or horror.</i>

00:16.660 --> 00:19.280
<i>I just have to categorize it as 
part of work and get through it.</i>

00:20.200 --> 00:22.200
<b>Silence...</b>

00:20.200 --> 00:22.660
<b>Out of Order</b>

00:26.220 --> 00:27.480
<i>Let's do this.</i>

01:58.510 --> 02:03.010
<b>#20 
Things You Don't Like</b>

02:00.940 --> 02:03.460
Why did I end up with the controller?

02:03.800 --> 02:06.510
It's better for someone who's 
never played it before to do it.

02:06.510 --> 02:07.980
We'll give you tips.

02:07.980 --> 02:08.730
Okay...

02:08.730 --> 02:09.300
<i>I hate this.</i>

02:10.170 --> 02:11.810
Here we go!

02:11.810 --> 02:12.950
<i>It's so realistic.</i>

02:12.950 --> 02:13.950
<i>I'm scared.</i>

02:14.780 --> 02:15.900
What are you doing?

02:15.900 --> 02:17.960
The controls are difficult.

02:15.900 --> 02:20.610
<b>Mash mash</b>

02:15.900 --> 02:20.610
<b>Mash mash</b>

02:17.960 --> 02:20.630
I've never seen someone struggle
 with just walking around.

02:20.910 --> 02:22.300
<i>I want to stop.</i>

02:22.300 --> 02:24.820
Oh, I got a handgun.

02:24.820 --> 02:26.330
All right, here it comes.

02:26.330 --> 02:27.480
Mima! Behind you!

02:27.710 --> 02:28.210
<b>Turn</b>

02:28.070 --> 02:30.160
Not there! In the game!

02:31.920 --> 02:32.750
<b>Jump</b>

02:33.080 --> 02:34.330
Shoot! Shoot!

02:34.710 --> 02:36.170
<b>Dwaddle dwaddle</b>

02:35.070 --> 02:36.310
Your HP is almost gone!

02:36.310 --> 02:37.160
What button is it?

02:40.880 --> 02:42.640
<b>Exhausted...</b>

02:40.880 --> 02:42.640
<b>Exhausted...</b>

02:42.020 --> 02:43.840
I've never seen Mima like this.

02:44.830 --> 02:46.580
Can I give it one more try?

02:46.580 --> 02:48.060
Sure, but are you all right?

02:48.470 --> 02:50.540
This is part of my job.

02:50.540 --> 02:52.930
You really do take your work seriously.

02:53.790 --> 02:54.850
Oh, wow!

02:54.850 --> 02:56.360
You missed every shot!

02:56.360 --> 02:57.530
What happened to your aim?

02:57.530 --> 02:59.230
Weren't you in the archery club?!

02:59.230 --> 03:02.410
That was ten years ago...

03:02.360 --> 03:05.740
<b>Slam slam</b>

03:02.410 --> 03:05.740
You know you can shoot without 
moving the controller around?

03:06.450 --> 03:07.900
I'm exhausted.

03:07.900 --> 03:09.230
Good work.

03:09.230 --> 03:11.110
That's about par for a beginner.

03:11.110 --> 03:13.120
Yeah, you did good.

03:13.510 --> 03:15.700
I'm going to go take out my contacts.

03:15.700 --> 03:17.970
Sure. Can I play next?

03:19.930 --> 03:21.990
<i>I feel like I might dream 
about this tonight...</i>

03:22.380 --> 03:24.090
<b>Silence...</b>

03:24.080 --> 03:26.680
<i>Are the lights out?</i>

03:24.600 --> 03:25.430
<b>Wave wave</b>

03:24.970 --> 03:26.680
<b>Motion
sensor
lights</b>

03:24.970 --> 03:26.680
<b>Motion
sensor
lights</b>

03:27.450 --> 03:28.640
<i>Whatever.</i>

03:28.930 --> 03:30.900
<i>I'm just taking my contacts out.</i>

03:42.820 --> 03:44.030
<b>Appear...</b>

03:45.780 --> 03:46.870
<b>Refreshed</b>

03:47.170 --> 03:49.820
<i>Being in a darkened bathroom is so relaxing.</i>

03:50.250 --> 03:53.210
<b>Water running</b>

03:51.080 --> 03:53.210
<i>Wasn't there someone else in here?</i>

03:51.250 --> 03:53.210
<b>Turn turn</b>

03:53.850 --> 03:55.170
This is so fun!

03:54.670 --> 03:55.380
<b>Bang!!</b>

03:54.670 --> 03:55.380
<b>Bang!!</b>

03:54.670 --> 03:55.380
<b>Open</b>

03:55.670 --> 03:56.380
<b>Slam!</b>

03:55.670 --> 03:56.380
<b>Close</b>

03:57.380 --> 03:58.230
Huh?

03:58.230 --> 04:00.580
Mima, your contacts are still in.

04:00.580 --> 04:01.360
Senpai.

04:01.360 --> 04:01.910
Yes?

04:02.340 --> 04:05.500
May I please work from your home tonight?

04:05.500 --> 04:06.240
What?

04:06.240 --> 04:08.390
So I can ask you right away 
if I have a question?

04:08.390 --> 04:11.280
I mean, my little brother will 
be there too. Is that okay?

04:11.280 --> 04:11.810
Sure.

04:11.810 --> 04:13.860
The more, the better.

04:13.860 --> 04:14.880
What does that mean?

04:14.880 --> 04:17.940
Ah, Mima doesn't want to 
go home where he's alone.

04:17.940 --> 04:20.980
He must have really gone 
above and beyond today.

04:22.040 --> 04:23.820
Oh, it's Mima-san!

04:24.310 --> 04:25.320
Hello.

04:25.320 --> 04:27.030
He said he's spending the night.

04:27.330 --> 04:29.070
Sorry for the short notice.

04:29.070 --> 04:30.910
It's fine. I'm glad you're here!

04:31.420 --> 04:33.000
In fact, this is perfect.

04:33.280 --> 04:38.220
The "Scary Things That Actually Happened"
 summer break special is about to start.

04:38.560 --> 04:41.090
Ooh, "Scary Actually" was today?

04:41.090 --> 04:42.350
Let's watch it together.

04:42.350 --> 04:43.500
I'll be going home now.

04:43.500 --> 04:44.590
Already?!

04:44.870 --> 04:47.100
Yes. Thank you so much.

04:47.470 --> 04:50.060
<b>Time stayed:</b>

04:47.470 --> 04:50.060
<b>1 minute</b>

04:51.950 --> 04:54.140
<i>Now what do I do?</i>

04:54.140 --> 04:57.450
<i>I'm not really relishing the idea of 
spending the whole night outside.</i>

04:57.450 --> 05:01.350
<i>Is there somewhere more
 comforting I could relax?</i>

05:02.640 --> 05:03.870
<i>Comforting?</i>

05:04.740 --> 05:05.910
Mima-san?

05:05.150 --> 05:06.700
<b>Comforting</b>

05:05.910 --> 05:06.700
Good evening.

05:06.700 --> 05:07.920
Good evening.

05:07.920 --> 05:09.160
Sorry for the short notice.

05:09.510 --> 05:12.330
I was surprised to get a 
message from you so suddenly.

05:12.330 --> 05:13.500
Please come in.

05:13.500 --> 05:14.740
Thank you for having me.

05:17.000 --> 05:18.770
You didn't get lost on 
the way here, did you?

05:18.770 --> 05:20.710
No, it was actually quite close.

05:21.170 --> 05:23.490
It's weird for me to say this,
 since I'm the one who asked,

05:23.490 --> 05:25.550
but I'm suprised you agreed.

05:25.970 --> 05:27.500
I'll explain the reason later.

05:27.500 --> 05:28.600
Please let me stay the night.

05:28.600 --> 05:29.170
Wha?

05:29.490 --> 05:30.880
Well, you see...

05:31.270 --> 05:33.080
I already had a visitor.

05:33.080 --> 05:35.070
Mima-san really came.

05:35.070 --> 05:36.340
Shun-kun?

05:36.950 --> 05:38.710
I hope I'm not interrupting.

05:38.710 --> 05:40.160
It's not a problem.

05:40.160 --> 05:42.140
I'm just getting some help with my homework.

05:42.140 --> 05:42.910
Oh, right.

05:42.910 --> 05:44.560
It's summer break for students.

05:44.830 --> 05:46.660
I was planning on going home when it was done,

05:46.660 --> 05:47.940
but it never ends.

05:48.840 --> 05:52.030
Homework assigned for summer break 
can't be finished in one day...

05:52.030 --> 05:54.160
<i>Being a student isn't easy either.</i>

05:54.470 --> 05:56.430
Should I help, too?

05:56.430 --> 05:59.270
Huh? It's not like you would 
do my homework, right?

05:59.270 --> 06:01.570
I could maybe explain the 
parts you don't understand.

06:01.570 --> 06:03.990
Then that's not going to 
make it go any faster.

06:03.990 --> 06:08.760
Oh, since I didn't know you
 were here, I only bought two.

06:09.320 --> 06:11.880
Sugar is ideal when you're studying,

06:11.880 --> 06:13.440
so you two should have these.

06:12.390 --> 06:15.100
<b></b>Pudding
With
Heart

06:13.440 --> 06:15.100
The expensive pudding from 
the place by the station?!

06:15.580 --> 06:18.310
I'm not going to invite myself 
over and come empty-handed.

06:18.310 --> 06:19.810
You're a god!

06:19.810 --> 06:21.250
Thank you very much.

06:21.250 --> 06:21.930
Huh?

06:22.300 --> 06:24.970
It looks like they forgot 
to include the spoons.

06:24.970 --> 06:27.680
I can bring some spoons.

06:27.680 --> 06:28.640
Thank you.

06:29.040 --> 06:29.860
Here you go.

06:29.860 --> 06:32.720
Thanks. Mind if I start eating?

06:32.720 --> 06:33.400
Go ahead.

06:33.660 --> 06:35.280
<i>When I look at Shun-kun,</i>

06:35.280 --> 06:36.820
<i>it feels like I have a nephew.</i>

06:37.090 --> 06:38.620
Thanks for the snack!

06:40.330 --> 06:40.460
<b>Clink</b>

06:40.710 --> 06:40.830
<b>Clink</b>

06:41.170 --> 06:41.290
<b>Clink</b>

06:41.540 --> 06:41.670
<b>Clink</b>

06:41.920 --> 06:41.960
<b>Clink</b>

06:42.040 --> 06:43.170
<b>Turn turn</b>

06:43.420 --> 06:43.540
<b>Clink</b>

06:43.750 --> 06:45.380
Don't you have any smaller spoons?

06:44.040 --> 06:44.170
<b>Clink</b>

06:44.670 --> 06:44.800
<b>Clink</b>

06:45.300 --> 06:45.420
<b>Clink</b>

06:45.380 --> 06:48.810
Sorry, I don't ever really need them, 
so I always forget to buy any.

06:45.670 --> 06:50.970
<b>Turn turn</b>

06:48.810 --> 06:50.980
I just use the big spoons instead.

06:50.980 --> 06:53.140
<i>I messed up.</i>

06:51.430 --> 06:51.550
<b>Clink</b>

06:52.050 --> 06:52.180
<b>Clink</b>

06:52.680 --> 06:52.800
<b>Clink</b>

06:53.410 --> 06:57.080
I'll go to the convenience store and get 
some spoons while I get something to drink.

06:57.080 --> 06:58.330
Then why don't I...

06:58.330 --> 06:59.160
I'll go!

06:59.160 --> 07:00.800
I'm tired from sitting all this time, anyway!

07:01.390 --> 07:02.370
Here you go.

07:02.370 --> 07:04.410
Use this, and buy whatever you want.

07:04.410 --> 07:06.090
Seriously? Awesome!

07:06.090 --> 07:07.950
It's late, so be careful.

07:08.580 --> 07:11.110
Don't follow any strangers.

07:11.110 --> 07:13.870
Do you think I'm, like... five?

07:13.990 --> 07:17.040
<b>See you later.</b>

07:13.990 --> 07:17.040
<b>See you later.</b>

07:15.020 --> 07:17.030
Thank you for doing all this.

07:17.030 --> 07:19.230
No, I'm the one who invited myself.

07:19.640 --> 07:23.360
It's nice that you have a convenience 
store right next to your apartment.

07:23.360 --> 07:24.250
Yes.

07:24.250 --> 07:26.720
But that means I end up
 buying most of my meals there.

07:26.720 --> 07:27.960
That makes sense.

07:28.500 --> 07:32.580
<i>Didn't Motoharu say he was renting 
a room somewhere around here too?</i>

07:32.580 --> 07:36.560
So what brings you here so suddenly?

07:37.810 --> 07:40.230
<i>I shouldn't lie to the kid who's 
putting me up for the night,</i>

07:40.230 --> 07:42.220
<i>but I can't disclose what 
I'm working on either.</i>

07:42.690 --> 07:46.180
Well, I was playing a horror 
game with a friend.

07:46.180 --> 07:46.930
You were?

07:47.290 --> 07:49.240
So you're a gamer, too?

07:49.240 --> 07:50.920
I love gaming.

07:50.920 --> 07:53.010
<i>That's another thing we have in common!</i>

07:53.010 --> 07:55.140
Oh, no, I'm no good at games.

07:55.140 --> 07:57.270
Sorry for jumping to conclusions.

07:57.160 --> 07:58.410
<b>Sad</b>

07:57.270 --> 07:58.420
<i>I was wrong.</i>

07:59.410 --> 08:01.390
<i>I'm such a pathetic adult.</i>

08:01.390 --> 08:02.760
It's embarassing to admit it,

08:02.760 --> 08:04.780
but I'm not really great with horror either.

08:04.780 --> 08:06.700
Instead of being home by myself,

08:06.700 --> 08:09.260
I was hoping to hang out 
with someone who could distract me.

08:09.650 --> 08:11.130
<i>Is he disappointed in me now?</i>

08:11.130 --> 08:13.990
Oh, so that's why you wanted to stay over.

08:13.680 --> 08:15.840
<b>Casually cool...</b>

08:13.990 --> 08:15.850
Uh, that's right.

08:16.270 --> 08:19.230
So I guess even you have 
things you don't like.

08:19.230 --> 08:21.820
You're always helping me out,

08:22.180 --> 08:25.750
so it's really nice to be able 
to help you out for once.

08:26.520 --> 08:33.990
<b>Comforting</b>

08:27.170 --> 08:31.600
I feel like scary things would avoid you.

08:31.600 --> 08:33.130
Really?

08:33.130 --> 08:34.490
I can't sense anything supernatural, though.

08:34.490 --> 08:36.550
Somehow I feel better now.

08:36.910 --> 08:38.940
I feel like I can work hard again tomorrow.

08:39.410 --> 08:40.900
Thank you so much.

08:40.900 --> 08:42.950
But I really didn't do anything.

08:42.950 --> 08:45.370
By the way, Shun-kun's 
taking a long time, huh.

08:45.370 --> 08:46.980
Now that you mention it...

08:47.460 --> 08:49.420
<b>Alone...</b>

08:48.060 --> 08:51.340
<i>Crap. What was Hayate-san's 
apartment number again?</i>

08:51.340 --> 08:53.180
<i>I left my phone there, too.</i>

08:53.180 --> 08:55.230
<i>Maybe he'll realize and come down.</i>

08:59.510 --> 09:00.930
A crow.

09:00.930 --> 09:03.900
Mima, you don't really like 
things like this, right?

09:03.900 --> 09:05.470
You don't have to force yourself.

09:05.470 --> 09:07.520
It's fine.

09:07.520 --> 09:10.790
I don't want to do PR for a product 
I have no experience with.

09:10.790 --> 09:14.050
I think it will lead to a 
perspective from people like me,

09:14.050 --> 09:15.700
so I'll stick with it until the end.

09:16.090 --> 09:19.830
<i>Huh, looks like he's found balance.</i>

09:19.830 --> 09:23.500
<i>I guess he got better at finding 
things that are soothing to him.</i>

09:26.030 --> 09:27.740
The enthusiasm is there,

09:27.740 --> 09:29.600
but your gaming skills still suck.

11:00.010 --> 11:05.010
<b>Coming up next</b>

11:00.010 --> 11:05.010
<b>Friends</b>

11:05.020 --> 11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

11:05.020 --> 11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
